From: SPNMX57 OpenWrt port
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca: add QCA8386 (Manhattan) switch driver

Hook up the QCA8386 DSA driver carried in files/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8386.c.
The QCA8386 pairs a qca8k-family switch core with four QCA8084 2.5G PHYs and
an NSS clock controller, all behind one indirect MDIO window. qca8k cannot
drive it: the page register and the upper-16-bit register decode differ.

The driver comes from https://github.com/louij2/linksys-spnmx57-openwrt
(60746fd9b347, OpenWrt PR #25902), where it runs on the IPQ5018-based Linksys
SPNMX57. Here it is used for the Cudy WR11000 (IPQ5322).
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/Kconfig
@@ -24,3 +24,12 @@
 	help
 	  This enabled support for LEDs present on the Qualcomm Atheros
 	  QCA8K Ethernet switch chips.
+
+config NET_DSA_QCA8386
+	tristate "Qualcomm QCA8386 (Manhattan) Ethernet switch support"
+	depends on NET_DSA
+	select NET_DSA_TAG_QCA
+	select REGMAP
+	help
+	  This enables support for the Qualcomm QCA8386 ("Manhattan"/MHT)
+	  Ethernet switch, as found on the Linksys SPNMX57 and Cudy WR11000.
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/Makefile
@@ -5,3 +5,4 @@
 ifdef CONFIG_NET_DSA_QCA8K_LEDS_SUPPORT
 qca8k-y				+= qca8k-leds.o
 endif
+obj-$(CONFIG_NET_DSA_QCA8386)	+= qca8386.o
